      "writtenOn": "2023-03-17T01:21:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There are register groups for the various sections of the retimer (DP, TBT, USB4, etc). The group of registers in the TopCtl section are what are used to control the operation modes of the ANX7452. The device addresses for these registers are stored themselves in the TOP register section, and it\u0027s only TOP registers that are access via the chips main I2C device address which is selected via the 2 addr strapping pins. \n\n0x40 is the 8 bit default I2C address for the TopCtl section of registers. I think it is safest to use the value stored in [Top:0x91] as opposed to having it hard coded as a macro.",
      "parentUuid": "b5d11282_271db8a1",
      "revId": "f849cf5122d00933a0d23ffe12dc59cd05d0353e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
